<Positioned left="48" top="1078" width="1704"><Container alignment="CENTER_LEFT"><Text fontSize="11" color="#6C7C99FF" fontFamily="Noto Sans Mono CJK SC" fontStyle="NORMAL">SOURCES  S1 NASA Ozone Watch — Annual Records (Antarctic) · S2 NASA Ozone Watch — What is the Ozone Hole?</Text></Container></Positioned>
<Positioned left="48" top="1096" width="1704"><Container alignment="CENTER_LEFT"><Text fontSize="11" color="#6C7C99FF" fontFamily="Noto Sans Mono CJK SC" fontStyle="NORMAL">The 220 DU threshold is the published definition of the hole. Bar length is derived here as 220 DU minus that year's published minimum daily column ozone, so it is a computed quantity, not a separate measurement.</Text></Container></Positioned>
<Positioned left="48" top="1118"><Text fontSize="11" color="#6C7C99FF" fontFamily="Noto Sans Mono CJK SC" fontStyle="NORMAL">STRATOSPHERE REVIEW · ISSUE 07 · FIG. 03</Text></Positioned>
